  "id": "Compound::DB01118 - Gene::1551",
  "verbalization": "Amiodarone, a known inhibitor of Cytochrome P450 2D6 (CYP2D6), is linked to Cyp3a7 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Amiodarone, as part of the CYP2D6 inhibitors class, interacts with Ritonavir and Quinidine, both of which bind to Cyp3a7. This indicates a potential mechanism where CYP2D6 inhibitors may influence Cyp3a7 through direct binding, possibly altering its activity or expression. The shared lowest common ancestor between Amiodarone and Ritonavir, as well as between Amiodarone and Quinidine, points to a common functional pathway involving cytochrome enzymes and their regulatory roles. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on CYP3A7 in the metabolic processes affected by these drugs, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
